# {{ component.name }} — FastAPI backend

A src-layout Python package with an app factory, `GET /health` and HTTP boundary tests.
Authentication, databases, business use cases and deployment are not implemented. Add layers or interfaces only when
real responsibilities require them.

```bash
# From this package directory
uv sync --group dev
uv run pytest
uv build
# Start a development server only when needed; loopback only
uv run uvicorn {{ component.module }}.app:create_app --factory --host 127.0.0.1 --port 8000
```

Keep the generated `uv.lock` with this package. Python 3.11 or later is required; choose the actual minor version for
its toolchain and CI. Exact dependency pins were checked against PyPI on 2026-10-26:
[FastAPI](https://pypi.org/project/fastapi/0.162.0/), [Uvicorn](https://pypi.org/project/uvicorn/0.54.0/).
The current [Starlette TestClient guidance](https://starlette.dev/testclient/) uses `httpx2==2.16.0`, which requires
Python 3.11 or later.

## Ownership

- `src/{{ component.module }}/app.py`: app composition and the HTTP boundary; extract feature routers when needed.
- `tests/test_health.py`: software-only response/error smoke tests, not product acceptance, load or operations evidence.
- `pyproject.toml` / `uv.lock`: this package's dependencies and independent environment.
- Resources: define ownership and cleanup through lifespan/dependencies when actual resources are introduced.

